The **`mistral-small-latest`** model can take a document as input in a chat message for document QnA tasks. To pass a document, you can encode it in **Base64** and include it in the request using the `document_url` content type with a `data:application/pdf;base64,<base64_pdf>` URL format. Here’s how to do it in **cURL** or **Python** (though Python examples are not provided in the sources for this specific case, the cURL example is sufficient) [2].

### Example cURL Request
```bash
curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${MISTRAL_API_KEY}" \
  -d '{
    "model": "mistral-small-latest",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "what is the last sentence in the document"
          },
          {
            "type": "document_url",
            "document_url": "data:application/pdf;base64,<base64_pdf>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }'
```

Alternatively, you can upload a PDF to Mistral’s Cloud and retrieve a signed URL for QnA [2].

